R"VG(
# ledger_report.vg (H-04's second pass): the industrial age's papers of business and learning: a works' ledger (its wages and its coal
# in the people's coin), a scientific report on what that world has to measure (its moons, its comet, its rivers, its fields), a
# patent, a pinned bundle of telegrams, a works' rules. Each in the people's own trades and goods.

# ---- the ledger ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.ledger (words=24..110)
  {ledger.head} {ledger.items}. {ledger.end}
  {ledger.head} {ledger.items}. {ledger.note} {ledger.end}

ledger.head (formula)
  The accounts of the {$home} {ledger.what}, {season.now} of the year {#year:digits}:
  Paid out and taken in, the {ledger.what} at {$home}:
  The {ledger.what}, {$home}: the book for {season.now}.
  Received and spent by the {ledger.what} of {$home}, year {#year:digits}:

ledger.what (people=4)
  mill
  works
  store
  school
  brewery
  {crop} mill
  {craft} works
  fire company
  hospital
  dye house
  ropewalk
  {festival} committee
  (inv.railway=1) railway yard
  (coast=1) boat yard

ledger.items
  {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}
  {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}
  {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}; {ledger.item}

ledger.item
  (once) wages, {n} hands at {n} {coin} a week
  (once) {fuel}, {nbig} {measure.load}
  (once) to the doctor, for the boy in the yard
  (once) received for {crop}, {nbig} {coin}
  (once) repairs to the roof, again
  (once) oil for the engine, {n} drums
  (once) owed by the council since {season.next} last year, still owing
  (once) lamp oil, {n} barrels
  (once) lost to the flood, written off
  (once) to the widow of the man killed at the press, {n} {coin} a month
  (once) the new boiler, the first payment of {n}
  (once) {vessel}, {nbig}, from the {craft} yard
  (once) a gift to {holyplace} for {festival}
  (once) fines, {n} {smallcoin}, the hands being late
  (once) feed for the {herd}, {n} {measure.load}
  (once) {drink} for the hands at {festival}, by custom
  (once) received for {craft} goods sent to {city2}, {nbig} {coin}
  (once) a new {ind.tool.n}, the old one past mending
  (once) the night watchman, {n} {smallcoin} a night
  (once) postage and the clerk's ink
  (once) the rates, paid under protest
ledger.note
  The {herd} kept in the yard are not ours and will be charged for.
  The clerk is short by {n} {smallcoin} and has paid it from his own pocket.
  The {crop} sent to {city2} is not yet paid for.
  (stage>=1) Less in than out, the fourth season running.
# a book's closing words, as the clerk of each house keeps them
ledger.end (formula people=2)
  Balance carried to the next page.
  The books do not balance and I do not know why. Checked twice.
  Signed, the clerk.
  Examined and found correct, with one exception, noted.
  Carried forward, the ink being low.
  Closed for the season, by the clerk's hand.
ind.tool.n
  anvil
  loom
  press
  saw
  wheel
  cart

# ---- the scientific report -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.report (words=30..160)
  {report.head}\n{report.what}\n{report.method}\n{report.find}\n{report.end}
  {report.head}\n{report.what} {report.why}\n{report.method} {report.method2}\n{report.find}\n{report.end}

report.head (formula)
  (has:academy) To {academy}: a report from {$home}, the {#year:ord} year of {city}.
  (has:university) Read before {university} in {season.now}, year {#year:digits}.
  A report on observations made at {$home}, year {#year:digits}.
  Observations at {$home}, communicated to the learned of {city}.

report.what
  (comet=1) The writer has followed the hairy star through {season.now} and offers its path{report.x.purpose}.
  (moons>0) The writer has measured the motions of {moon} over {n} years{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has kept the record of the weather at {$home} for {#nbig|year}{report.x.purpose}.
  (desert=1) The writer has measured how far the sand has moved since the old survey{report.x.purpose}.
  (giant=1) The writer has watched the wanderer through the new lens{report.x.purpose}.
  (rings=1) The writer has measured the shadow of the ring on the land through a whole year{report.x.purpose}.
  (aurora=1) The writer has counted the nights of the northern lights at {$home} and set them beside the weather{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has measured the fall of {river} at {$home} in every season{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has counted the {tree} on the slopes of {mountain} and compared the count with the old maps{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has weighed the {crop} of {n} fields, some manured and some not, over {n} seasons{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has followed the {bird} on their passage over {$home} for {#nbig|year}{report.x.purpose}.
  (coast=1) The writer has measured the tides at {$home} against the phases of {skyone}{report.x.purpose}.
  (economy=herding|economy2=herding) The writer has bred the {herd} of {$home} for size and for temper, and reports on both.
  The writer has measured the heat of the springs below {mountain}{report.x.purpose}.
  (geysers=1) The writer has timed the hot springs that throw water into the air, and finds them a clock.
  (glowflora=1) The writer has studied the light of the lamp trees, which goes out when they are cut.
  (saltflats=1) The writer has measured how fast the salt flats dry after the rains{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has counted the catch of {fish} at {$home}, season by season, against the warmth of the water{report.x.purpose}.
  The writer has measured the {fruit} of one orchard, tree by tree, for {n} years{report.x.purpose}.
report.why
  The work was begun by the writer's teacher and is finished here, {report.x.when}.
  The question was put to the writer by the {report.x.askers}, who wanted an answer and not a report.
  It has long been said at {$home} that {report.saying}; the writer wished to know if it was so.
report.x.askers
  farmers
  fishers
  {craft} masters
  priests of {holyplace}
report.saying
  the {bird} know the weather before the almanac
  {mountain} smokes before a hard winter
  the {crop} grows best under a waning moon
  the river remembers its old course
  the {herd} lie down before rain
  {fish} run when the {tree} flower
  a wet {festival} means a dry harvest
  the springs are warmer in the years of the hairy star
report.method
  The observations were made {report.x.where}, {report.x.when}, {report.x.with}.
  The instruments were checked against those of {city}, and found {report.x.agree}.
  The figures are given in {report.x.where2}, {report.x.tables}.
  (inv.photography=1) The plates are kept at {$home} and may be seen by anyone who asks, {report.x.tables}.
  (inv.lens=1) A lens was ground for the purpose by the writer, from {report.x.glass}, and will not be ground again.
  Every reading was taken twice, {report.x.when}, once by the writer and once by an assistant who is more careful.
  (inv.telegraph=1) The times were compared by wire with the observatory at {city}, {report.x.when}.
report.method2
  The {measure.far} are those of the old survey.
  Where the readings disagree, both are given, and the writer's preference is marked in {colour.any} ink.
  The writer was ill in {season.any} and the readings of those weeks are a neighbour's, a {report.x.neighbour}.
  The work was paid for by the {craft} guild, which wishes it known.
report.x.where
  from the roof of the {$home} school
  from the tower of {holyplace}
  on the hill above {$home}
  in a boat on {river}
  in the writer's garden, among the {veg}
  from the top of the {craft} works' chimney, with permission
report.x.when
  at night
  at first light and at dusk
  every day at noon
  in every season
  on the first night of each month
  {time.of}
report.x.with
  with the help of two students who did not complain
  with a borrowed lens
  with a clock that loses a minute a day
  with instruments made by a {report.x.neighbour}
  with the patience of the writer's family
report.x.neighbour
  smith
  glassblower
  clockmaker
  carpenter
  miller
report.x.agree
  in agreement
  wrong by a little
  wrong by a great deal
  older than the writer
report.x.tables
  with the writer's notes in the margin
  in the writer's own hand
  for anyone with the patience to read them
report.x.glass
  a bottle of {drink}
  the window of {holyplace}
  good glass from {city}
report.find
  The writer finds {report.x.found}, and {report.x.ask}.
  The writer finds {report.x.found}; {report.x.ask2}.
  (stage>=0) The writer finds the change steady and in one direction only, and asks that the council be told.
report.x.found
  the change greater than expected, and greater each year
  nothing that the old reckoning did not predict
  the figures irregular
  that the old saying is half right
  a period of {n} years in the figures
  the instruments of {city} wrong by a little
  the {crop} heavier in the years after a hard winter
  the {bird} early when {skyone} is low
  the river higher by a hand than in the old survey
  the {herd} of the high farms larger than those of the valleys
  {fish} fewer in the years the river is low
  the {fruit} earlier by a week in the town than in the fields
report.x.ask
  asks that others repeat the work
  asks that the council be told
  will say more when the funds allow
  has written to the learned of {city}
  cannot say what keeps it
report.x.ask2
  the writer does not know why, and says so
  which is itself remarkable
  the farmers of {$home} say they could have told the writer
  a second paper will follow
report.end (formula)
  Respectfully submitted.
  The writer thanks the keepers of the {$home} school for the use of the roof.
  Further observations will follow if the funds allow.
  The writer will answer letters, but slowly.

# ---- the patent ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
genre.patent (words=25..80)
  {@event invention patent 25}

patent.invention
  (has:$e.a) {patent.head} {$e.a:name} of {$e.place}, for {$e.invention}, {patent.as}. {patent.claim} {patent.claim} {patent.end}
  (has:$e.a) {patent.head} {$e.a:name}, a {$e.a.trade} of {$e.place}, for {$e.invention}, being new and useful. {patent.claim} {patent.end}
  (!has:$e.a) {patent.head} the makers of {$e.place}, for {$e.invention}, {patent.as}. {patent.claim} {patent.claim} {patent.end}
patent.none
  {patent.head} {patent.small} {patent.claim} {patent.end}
  {patent.head} {patent.small} {patent.claim} {patent.claim} {patent.end}

patent.head (formula)
  Letters of patent, granted at {$seat}, year {#year:digits}:
  A patent is granted to
  By the office of patents at {$seat}, the {#year:ord} year of {city}, a patent to

patent.small
  a maker of {$home}, for an improved {patent.thing}.
  the {$home} works, for a new kind of {patent.thing}.
  a {patent.who} of {$home}, for a {patent.thing} {patent.purpose}.
patent.who
  smith
  carpenter
  widow
  schoolmaster
  miller
  clockmaker
patent.thing (people=6)
  pump
  lamp
  plough
  loom
  lock for doors
  stove that does not smoke
  boiler that does not burst
  churn
  press for {crop2}
  mill for {crop}
  cradle that rocks itself
  boot for the wet
  trap for {pest}
  oven
  wheel
  bell for {holyplace}
  frame for the {craft} trade
  basket that folds
patent.purpose
  for the use of farmers
  worked by one hand
  for the {craft} trade
  for houses without a chimney
  to run on {fuel}

patent.claim
  (once) It does the work of {n} men and asks for nothing but {fuel}.
  (once) It may be made by any {patent.maker} with the drawings attached and {patent.tools}.
  (once) It is safer than the {patent.old} it replaces, which is not saying much.
  (once) It has been tried at {$home} for {n} months without failing, in {weather.now}.
  (once) No other may make it for {#number|year}, on pain of a fine of {n} {coin}.
  (once) It saves a third of the {fuel} and all of the temper.
  (once) It can be taken apart and carried by one of the {herd}.
  (once) Its parts are listed in the schedule, all {n} of them, with their prices in {coin}.
  (once) It was shown at the {festival} fair and drew a crowd that broke a stall of the {craft} row.
patent.old
  {ind.tool.p}
  way of the old {craft} masters
  thing the grandmothers used

ind.tool.p
  quern
  hand loom
  bucket and rope
  old stove

patent.end (formula)
  Drawings attached.
  Witnessed by the clerk of patents.
  The fee has been paid.
  Entered in the register.
report.x.purpose
  , for the farmers of {$home}
  , as the old {craft} masters kept their books
  , in the hope of a pattern
  , which nobody had done since the founding
  , at the request of the council
  , at the writer's own expense
  , with a {report.x.neighbour}'s help
report.x.where2
  the tables attached
  the ledger of the {craft} guild, by its leave
  the margins of the temple's book
  the tables attached, on {n} sheets
patent.maker
  smith
  clockmaker
  glassblower
  carpenter
  instrument maker
  good apprentice
patent.as
  as described in the schedule
  in the form of the model shown at {festival}
  after {n} years of trials at {$home}
  worked by {fuel}
  built at the {craft} works of {$home}
patent.tools
  {n} days' work
  a good fire
  patience
  the help of a {patent.maker}
)VG"
